Apple appears to be rolling out a new logo for Apple Music in its upcoming set of software updates. The logo has been spotted in both macOS 27.2 beta 3 and iOS 27.2 beta 3, and it's identical to the one that Apple used in its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/22/apple-music-hall-battersea-power-station/">Apple Music Hall announcement</a> last month.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-music-new-logo-red.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1068878" /><br/>
When Apple used the logo in the venue's press materials and on its new <a href="https://www.applemusichall.com/">official website</a>, it wasn't clear if this was a one-off branding exclusive to the hall. All the evidence now points to it being the company's official new logo for its music streaming service.<br/>
